Thanks @AI-Guru and @grunjol — I really appreciate the detailed review and independent testing.

@AI-Guru, good catch on the scroll issue inherited from PR #71. I verified that the stale `_savedPositions` restoration is still present in the legacy REST completion path. Remote Gateway turns do not use that completion block, but the compatibility REST mode can still reproduce the issue. I’ll follow the upstream fix and add a regression test before incorporating it into the fork.

@grunjol, the patch does not remove every `/v1/*` call globally. For Remote Gateway profiles, chat has been migrated: text, images, and files all use the same Dashboard WebSocket/JSON-RPC session, and `/v1/chat/completions` is not used on that path. The app still retains `/v1/models` and `/v1/chat/completions` for non-Desktop/legacy REST compatibility.

If the upstream direction is a complete Dashboard-only migration, I’d be happy to separate the transport work into smaller, reviewable contributions. Thanks again for taking the time to test it.

Hi @rusty4444,

A focused follow-up is now published as Hermes Android Community Remote Gateway 1.0.32.

This release fixes Android consumption of the optional `hermes.notification.delivery.v1` contract:

- notification reconciliation is independent from interaction-mode negotiation;
- the app reuses the existing authenticated session and does not start an agent/model run;
- `notification.pull` is parsed fail-closed and can retry after an empty or failed lifecycle attempt;
- repeated `(notification_id, version)` delivery is deduplicated;
- Android reports only the factual local delivery result and retains no semantic Notification authority;
- generic/older Gateways advertise no capability and receive zero notification RPCs.

The public release description is cumulative from the last public 1.0.13 baseline through 1.0.32, so it also documents the intervening chat, Activity Center, Projects, permissions, interaction modes, attachment, accessibility, and connection-form work.

Release and APKs:
https://github.com/CristianGCiocoi/hermes-android/releases/tag/hermesapk-test-1.0.32

Focused source PR and CI evidence:
https://github.com/CristianGCiocoi/hermes-android/pull/8

Validation: 417/417 Flutter tests, analyzer PASS, Android v2 signature verification PASS. The two APKs remain clearly labeled debug test builds. If useful upstream, I can continue to submit the generic Hermes portions as small focused PRs.
